# intel-gpu.drv's startup capabilities (docs/ccl-driver-manifests.md,
# docs/capability-handles.md). devmgr launches the driver and fills its
# startup table from these requests before it first runs; the driver reads
# them by binding name (Startup.Registers, ...). One MSI vector carries GT,
# GuC and display interrupts alike, as in i915 (no MSI-X on Gen12); it is
# optional while MSI stays disabled (no handler yet).
# Pages whose place inside BAR0 a manifest cannot name (forcewake, GGTT,
# reset, display, PHY and pipe pages) and the log publisher are runtime
# grants: the driver asks devmgr and the reply carries the capability.
(Executable_Manifest
  identity => "com.cubit.driver.intel-gpu"
  version => "0.1.0"
  drives => [(Device_Match.PCI_IDs (PCI_IDs 0x8086 0x46D0 0x46D4))]
  requests => [
    (device-memory "registers" 0 16777216 Access.Read)
    (interrupt "device" Interrupt_Mode.MSI 1)
    (service "device-manager" "device-manager")
    (service "filesystem" "firmware")
    (notification "gpu" Notify_Access.Manage "registration")]
  optional => ["registration" "firmware" "device"])
